item.description:
&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good stuff. Be kind to yourself while trying.  &lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Steve G&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I love where this list is coming from, but a lot of it feels upside down to me. &lt;br&gt;I have always felt that am not allowed to take up space, to speak or be heard and when I do I am probably annoying people so some of this list just reinforced the old patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I guess we have all been arseholes and will be again. Judgement is a sanctuary of sureness. Being sure is shoring up against a tsunami we could instead swim with and in. We could join everything in the swim; we will be swimming anyway even if we look away. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As to arseholism we will do it again - we can bear witness to our arseholism, acknowledge it, be sorry for it, offer compassion for it and try again.    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;
